  "body": "Part of #1509 (its body: \"What happens to the stand-alone Trochoidal slot operation (kept as a confined slot, or folded into Adaptive with old projects migrated) is recorded in the PR's decision file\").\n\nDecision taken unattended in #1509's PR (`docs/decisions/1509-adaptive-trochoid-method.md`, point 7): the stand-alone Trochoidal slot stays as it is - the confined slot #1503 made it (two points and a width, refused when it does not fit its selection). It is not folded into 2D Adaptive and no project is migrated.\n\nWhy it was kept: it cuts a slot the user places, which a region-driven method cannot express (a slot across open stock, a slot narrower than its face, a slot along a typed line). Folding it would need a project migration for a kind that shipped in v0.19.0.\n\nFor the maintainer to confirm or change:\n1. keep both (today), or\n2. retire the kind from the ribbon and open old projects as 2D Adaptive + Trochoidal where the slot equals its region, \"needs review\" otherwise, or\n3. keep the kind but rename it so it does not read as the adaptive strategy.\n\nRelated: #1517 (2D Pocket loses its Adaptive strategy), #1523 (one confine law for Slot and Trochoidal slot), #220.\n\nDone means: the maintainer's choice is recorded here; if it is 2 or 3, the work is filed as its own issue with a \"Done means\" line.\n",
